  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Dental Hygiene A.S. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 3, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7629/PublishedPdf), GE Pattern: SCC Local. Official Total Units: 96.5-98.5. PROGRAM STRUCTURE: Semesters 1-4 are program-eligibility prerequisites (labeled 'PreReq' on the map); Semesters 5-8 plus the Summer Session are the lockstep professional phase (labeled 'Maj'), and ALL DHYG major courses carry an enrollment limitation requiring acceptance into the Dental Hygiene program. Per the professional-phase convention, the prerequisites are collapsed here into a single pre-program block (n=1, 49 units) preserving their official Semester 1-4 sequence in this note — S1(Fall): ENGL, CHEM, PSYC C1000, ETHNS 300; S2(Spring): NUTRI, STAT/MATH, BIOL 430, SOC 300; S3(Fall): COMM, BIOL 431, Arts & Humanities; S4(Spring): BIOL 440, CHEM 306 (conditional) — and the professional phase is fully sequenced (n=2-6). This seed models the CHEM 305 + CHEM 306 path = 49+13+13+2+12+8.5 = 97.5 units (within the official 96.5-98.5; the low/high ends reflect the ENGL 3-4 and STAT/MATH 3-4 ranges). The alternative CHEM 309 path (5 units, skips CHEM 306 in S4) is documented in the chemistry choice notes. Financial-aid note from the map: students must claim Pre-Health Occupations as their major until accepted into the Dental Hygiene program. Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 (3) / ENGL 488 (4) / ESLW 340 (4); (2) CHEM 309 (Integrated General, Organic, and Biological Chemistry, 5) OR CHEM 305 (Introduction to Chemistry, 5) + CHEM 306 (5); (3) NUTRI 300 / NUTRI 480 Honors; (4) STAT C1000 (4) / STAT C1000H / MATH 300 (3); (5) COMM C1000 / COMM 331 / COMM 481 Honors. Prereqs per map: CHEM 305/309 require Elementary Algebra; BIOL 430 requires CHEM 305/309/400; BIOL 431 requires CHEM 305/309/400 and BIOL 430; BIOL 440 requires CHEM 305/309/400; CHEM 306 requires CHEM 305; DHYG 111 requires DHYG 103/107; DHYG 112/113/117 require DHYG 101/103/104/107/109; DHYG 129 requires DHYG 101; DHYG 121 requires DHYG 111/112/113/117/129; DHYG 131 requires DHYG 121/129; DHYG 134/135/138/139 require DHYG 121/127; DHYG 132 requires DHYG 127/129/131; DHYG 141/145/149 require DHYG 131/132/134/135/138/139. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
